solution_md:
Take 32 numbers  $a_1,a_2\dots a_{32}$   with\begin{align*}
a_i=Q\times P_{i,1}P_{i,2}\dots P_{i,32}
\end{align*}
Where  $P_{i,i}$  term is missing.For example,\begin{align*}
a_3=Q\times P_{3,1}P_{3,2}P_{3,4}\dots P_{3,32}
\end{align*}.
Here  $Q$  and all  $P$  are distinct odd primes.
Now,By CRT,take  $x$  such that,\begin{align*}
x&\equiv a_k\pmod{P_{i,k}}\ \ \ \forall i\ne k,\forall k
x&\not\equiv a_k\pmod{Q}\ \ \ \ \forall k
x&\not\equiv a_k\pmod{P_{k,i}}\ \forall i\ne k,\forall k
x&\equiv 1\pmod{2}
\end{align*}

Now write  $a_i,x-a_i$  in each of the 32 dominoes.

We need to show:

- $gcd(a_i,x-a_i)=1\ \ \ \forall i$
- $gcd(a_i,a_j)\ne 1\ \ \ \forall i\ne j$
- $gcd(x-a_i,x-a_j)\ne 1\ \ \ \forall i\ne j$
- $gcd(a_i,x-a_j)\ne1\ \ \ \forall i\ne j$
 $\bullet$  As all prime divisors of  $a_i$  namely, $Q,P_{i,1},P_{i,2},\dots P_{i,32}$  does not deide  $x-a_i$  does not devide  $x-a_i$  ,hence  $gcd(a_i,x-a_i)=1\ \ \ \forall i$ . $\bullet$  As  $Q|a_i,Q|a_j$  so  $gcd(a_i,a_j)\ne 1\ \ \ \forall i\ne j$ . $\bullet$  As  $x$  is odd by construction and  $a_i$  are also odd by construction,So  $2|gcd(x-a_i,x-a_j)$ . $\bullet$  Finally,by construction  $P_{i,j}| a_i$  and  $P_{i,j}|x-a_j$ .
Hence, $gcd(a_i,x-a_j)\ne1\ \ \ \forall i\ne j$   $\blacksquare$

