Marking angles, we find  $\angle{A'BC}=90-\beta, \angle{BCA'}=90-\theta, \angle{BA'C}=\beta+\theta, \angle{CA'T} =90-\beta$  (tangency),  $\angle{A'CT}=90+\theta$ . By Sinine Law in  $\triangle{BA'T}$  and  $\triangle{CA'T}$ , respectively: $\dfrac{BT}{cos\theta}=\dfrac{A'T}{cos\beta}$   $\Longrightarrow$   $A'T=\dfrac{BT\cdot{cos\beta}}{cos\theta }$   $\dfrac{CT}{cos\beta}=\dfrac{A'T}{cos\theta}$   $\Longrightarrow$   $A'T=\dfrac{CT\cdot{cos\theta}}{cos\beta }$  $\Longrightarrow$   $\boxed{\dfrac{BT}{CT}=(\dfrac{cos\theta}{cos\beta})^2}$ **Calculating  $\dfrac{CF}{BE}$ :**

