{Introduction}
We claim that the statement only works for  $n \equiv 0,1 (\mod 4)$ .
{Proof that 2,3 do not work}
note that LHS is  $\sum{|{x_i} - i|}$  and each value of  $x_i$  and  $i$  is counted once, whether in the positive or in the negative. Thus each number from  ${1,2,3...n}$  is counted j times where  $j \in [2,0,-2]$ . Thus LHS is even.  However note that non-negative integers only can appear in the RHS and no number  $\geq n$  can appear, so the set of numbers in RHS is [0,1,2,3,... $n-1$ ], so RHS  =  $\sum^{n-1}_{i = 0} {i} = \frac{n(n-1)}{2}$ , which is odd when  $n \equiv 2,3 (\mod 4).$ {construction for 0 mod 4}
