To do this, we define a way to push the regions around.

Notice that the regions can be placed in an  $n+1$  by  $n+1$  unit grid, and without loss of generality take a cell in the topmost column to be  $c_0$ , and the region containing it to be  $R_0$ , if it exists. We will define  $c_0,c_1,\dots,c_d$  and  $R_0,R_1,\dots,R_{d-1}$ . If  $R_0$  does not exist then we let  $d=0$ . Otherwise, we will construct these sequences in the following way using  $3$  cases.

Case  $1$ . We have the following configuration, where  $c_k$  is in green.

[asy]
