First, define  $E$  and  $F$  as the midpoints of  $BC$  and  $AB$  (respectively) and  $I_B$  as the  $B$ -excenter of triangle  $\Delta ABC$ .**Part 1:**  $OI\perp BD \implies AB+BC=2AC$ **Proof:** Clearly,  $OI\perp BD$  is equivalent to  $I$  being the midpoint of  $BD$ . It's well known that  $I_B$  is the reflection of  $I$  wrt  $D$ , and so  $BI=ID=DI_B$   $\implies$   $\tfrac{BI_B}{BI}=\tfrac{BI+ID+DI_B}{BI}=\tfrac{3BI}{BI}=3$ . It's also well known (just compare the inradius and  $B$ -exradius) that the homothety  $\Phi_1$  on  $B$  sending the incircle to the  $B$ -excircle has ratio  $\tfrac{AB+BC+AC}{AB+BC-AC}$ . It follows that  $\tfrac{BI_B}{BI}=3=\tfrac{AB+BC+AC}{AB+BC-AC}$   $\implies$   $3AB+3BC-3AC=AB+BC+AC$   $\implies$   $2AB+2BC=4AC$   $\implies$   $AB+BC=2AC$ .**Part 2:**  $AB+BC=2AC \implies OI\perp BD$ **Proof:** Note that the ratio of the homothety  $\Phi_1$  is  $\tfrac{AB+BC+AC}{AB+BC-AC}=\tfrac{3AC}{AC}=3$  and so  $\tfrac{BI_B}{BI}=3$   $\implies$   $BI_B=3BI$ . Since  $D$  is the midpoint of  $II_B$ , we have that  $BI+BI_B=2BD$   $\implies$   $4BI=2BD$   $\implies$   $2BI=BD$  and so  $I$  is the midpoint of  $BD$ , which completes the proof.

